#@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
#@type = "provisioning.security"

Feature:  Koroneiki to Provisioning Subscription Contact Worker Permissions
	Testing to assure that provisioning subscription contact worker permissions works properly.

Setup:
	* I get all test passwords and admin emails
	* I generate several static variables for Provisioning
	* I generate a provisioning company name
	* I generate a provisioning project name
	* I create a provisioning user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | provisioning.contact.worker                    |
	| Email Address | provisioning.contact.worker@liferay.com.broken |
	| First Name    | Provisioning                                   |
	| Last Name     | Contact Worker                                 |
	* I assign the provisioning user with the email address "provisioning.contact.worker@liferay.com.broken" to the provisioning role "Provisioning Contact Worker"
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | prm.koroneiki1                       |
	| Email Address | prm.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | PRM                                  |
	| Last Name     | Koroneiki1                           |
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | prm.koroneiki2                       |
	| Email Address | prm.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | PRM                                  |
	| Last Name     | Koroneiki2                           |

Teardown:
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Permis - ${staticProjectName}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I rename the first default user ID variable
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Misper - ${staticCompanyName}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I rename the second default user ID variable
	* I tear down the product consumptions on koroneiki made by the account "Permis - ${staticProjectName}" for the following products
	| DXP Production        |
	| Portal Production     |
	| Platinum Subscription |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following names
	| Permis - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Misper - ${staticCompanyName} |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following "Code" values
	| MISPERPERMIS |
	| MISPER       |
	* I tear down the projects with the following project codes via groovy
	| MISPERPERMIS |
	| MISPER       |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from okta
	| prm.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| prm.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from customer.liferay.com
	| prm.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| prm.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from koroneiki
	| prm.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| prm.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the contacts on koroneiki with the following email addresses
	| prm.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| prm.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I teardown the tickets with the following keywords from zendesk.liferay.com
	| New Subscription(s) for Permis - ${staticProjectName} |
	| New Subscription(s) for Misper - ${staticCompanyName} |
	* I obtain the IDs of the following user email addresses from zendesk.liferay.com
	| prm.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| prm.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I teardown users with the following userIds "${staticUserIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I obtain the external IDs of the following organizations from zendesk.liferay.com if still present
	| Permis - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Misper - ${staticCompanyName} |
	* I teardown organizations with the following organizationExternalIds "${staticOrganizationExternalIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId1}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId2}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from provisioning
	| provisioning.contact.worker@liferay.com.broken |

Scenario: View no subscription add button
	Testing the inability to add a new subscription 

	Given I publish a project with no partner RabbitMQ message with routing key "dossiera.provisioning.create" with the following values
	| Account Name                           | Misper - ${staticCompanyName}              |
	| Address City                           | Diamond Bar                                |
	| Address Country                        | United States                              |
	| Address Postal Code                    | 91765                                      |
	| Address Region                         | California                                 |
	| Address Street                         | 456 Fake Street                            |
	| Contact Email Address                  | prm.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken       |
	| Contact First Name                     | PRM                                        |
	| Contact Last Name                      | Koroneiki1                                 |
	| Dossiera Account Key                   | ${staticDossieraAccountKey}                |
	| Dossiera Address Key 1                 | ${staticDossieraAddressKey1}               |
	| Dossiera Address Key 2                 | ${staticDossieraAddressKey2}               |
	| Dossiera Contact Key                   | ${staticDossieraContactKey}                |
	| Dossiera Project Key                   | ${staticDossieraProjectKey}                |
	| End Day                                | ${staticEndDay}                            |
	| End Month                              | ${staticEndMonth}                          |
	| End Year                               | ${staticEndYear}                           |
	| Industry                               | Automotive                                 |
	| Owner Email Address                    | prm.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken       |
	| Owner First Name                       | PRM                                        |
	| Owner Last Name                        | Koroneiki2                                 |
	| Partner First Line Support             | false                                      |
	| Product Type                           | New                                        |
	| Product Name                           | Liferay Digital Enterprise - Prod Sizing 4 |
	| Project Name                           | Permis - ${staticProjectName}              |
	| Renewal                                | false                                      |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Key             | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityKey}          |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Line Item Key 1 | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityLineItemKey1} |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Line Item Key 2 | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityLineItemKey2} |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Sold By         | Liferay US                                 |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Stage Name      | Closed Won                                 |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Territory       | United States                              |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Type            | New Business                               |
	| Salesforce Owner User Key              | ${staticSalesforceOwnerUserKey}            |
	| Salesforce Project Key                 | ${staticSalesforceProjectKey}              |
	| Start Day                              | ${staticStartDay}                          |
	| Start Month                            | ${staticStartMonth}                        |
	| Start Year                             | ${staticStartYear}                         |
	| Subscription Level                     | Platinum                                   |
	| Version Number                         | 7.1                                        |
	And I log into the provisioning homepage as "provisioning.contact.worker@liferay.com.broken" with password "${staticProvisioningQaUserPassword}"
	And I update my password upon login to "test"
	And I go to the account index page
	And I search the accounts page using the keyword "Permis"
	And I click on the account with the name "Permis - ${staticProjectName}" on the provisioning index
	Then the add subscriptions button should not be present

Scenario: View subscription
	Testing the ability to add a subcription in koroneiki and viewing the subscription in the provisioning account details page 

	Given I publish a project with no partner RabbitMQ message with routing key "dossiera.provisioning.create" with the following values
	| Account Name                           | Misper - ${staticCompanyName}              |
	| Address City                           | Diamond Bar                                |
	| Address Country                        | United States                              |
	| Address Postal Code                    | 91765                                      |
	| Address Region                         | California                                 |
	| Address Street                         | 456 Fake Street                            |
	| Contact Email Address                  | prm.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken       |
	| Contact First Name                     | PRM                                        |
	| Contact Last Name                      | Koroneiki1                                 |
	| Dossiera Account Key                   | ${staticDossieraAccountKey}                |
	| Dossiera Address Key 1                 | ${staticDossieraAddressKey1}               |
	| Dossiera Address Key 2                 | ${staticDossieraAddressKey2}               |
	| Dossiera Contact Key                   | ${staticDossieraContactKey}                |
	| Dossiera Project Key                   | ${staticDossieraProjectKey}                |
	| End Day                                | ${staticEndDay}                            |
	| End Month                              | ${staticEndMonth}                          |
	| End Year                               | ${staticEndYear}                           |
	| Industry                               | Automotive                                 |
	| Owner Email Address                    | prm.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken       |
	| Owner First Name                       | PRM                                        |
	| Owner Last Name                        | Koroneiki2                                 |
	| Partner First Line Support             | false                                      |
	| Product Type                           | New                                        |
	| Product Name                           | Liferay Digital Enterprise - Prod Sizing 4 |
	| Project Name                           | Permis - ${staticProjectName}              |
	| Renewal                                | false                                      |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Key             | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityKey}          |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Line Item Key 1 | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityLineItemKey1} |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Line Item Key 2 | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityLineItemKey2} |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Sold By         | Liferay US                                 |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Stage Name      | Closed Won                                 |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Territory       | United States                              |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Type            | New Business                               |
	| Salesforce Owner User Key              | ${staticSalesforceOwnerUserKey}            |
	| Salesforce Project Key                 | ${staticSalesforceProjectKey}              |
	| Start Day                              | ${staticStartDay}                          |
	| Start Month                            | ${staticStartMonth}                        |
	| Start Year                             | ${staticStartYear}                         |
	| Subscription Level                     | Platinum                                   |
	| Version Number                         | 7.1                                        |
	And I generate static start and end dates
	And I generate static full start and end dates
	And I update a product purchase on koroneiki made by the account "Permis - ${staticProjectName}" for the product "DXP Production" to have the following values
	| End Date          | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual         | false                    | |
	| Start Date        | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status            | Approved                 | |
	And I update a product purchase on koroneiki made by the account "Permis - ${staticProjectName}" for the product "Platinum Subscription" to have the following values
	| End Date          | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual         | false                    | |
	| Start Date        | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status            | Approved                 | |
	And I create a product consumption for an account with the name "Permis - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "DXP Production" on koroneiki with the following values
	| Product Purchase        | true            |                |
	| Product Field and Value | additionalProp1 | propertyValue1 |
	| Product Field and Value | additionalProp2 | propertyValue2 |
	| Product Field and Value | additionalProp3 | propertyValue3 |
	And I log into the provisioning homepage as "provisioning.contact.worker@liferay.com.broken" with password "${staticProvisioningQaUserPassword}"
	And I update my password upon login to "test"
	And I go to the account index page
	And I search the accounts page using the keyword "Permis"
	And I click on the account with the name "Permis - ${staticProjectName}" on the provisioning index
	Then I should be able to view the product with the name "DXP Production" and the following values on the account details page
	| Name                  | DXP Production                                        |
	| Support Life          | ${staticFullStartDate} - ${staticFullOriginalEndDate} |
	| Grace Period End Date | ${staticFullEndDate}                                  |
	| Current Provisioned   | 1                                                     |
	| Current Purchased     | 1                                                     |
	| State                 | ACTIVE                                                |
	And I should be able to view the product with the name "DXP Production" under the "Primary" section
	And I should be able to view the product with the name "Platinum Subscription" and the following values on the account details page
	| Name                  | Platinum Subscription                                 |
	| Support Life          | ${staticFullStartDate} - ${staticFullOriginalEndDate} |
	| Grace Period End Date | ${staticFullEndDate}                                  |
	| Current Provisioned   | 0                                                     |
	| Current Purchased     | 1                                                     |
	| State                 | ACTIVE                                                |
	And I should be able to view the product with the name "Platinum Subscription" under the "Regular" section
	And the "Active" product tab should have the count value "2"
	And the "Future" product tab should have the count value "0"
	And the "Complimentary" product tab should have the count value "0"
	And the "Expired" product tab should have the count value "0"
	And the "Cancelled" product tab should have the count value "0"
	And the "All" product tab should have the count value "2"
	When I select the following products under the subscriptions tab
	| DXP Production        |
	| Platinum Subscription |
	Then the edit subscriptions button should not be present
	And the subscriptions action dropdown button should not be present
	When I click on the "Future" product tab
	Then I should not be able to view the product with the name "DXP Production" on the account details page
	And I should not be able to view the product with the name "Platinum Subscription" on the account details page
	When I click on the "Complimentary" product tab
	Then I should not be able to view the product with the name "DXP Production" on the account details page
	And I should not be able to view the product with the name "Platinum Subscription" on the account details page
	When I click on the "Expired" product tab
	Then I should not be able to view the product with the name "DXP Production" on the account details page
	And I should not be able to view the product with the name "Platinum Subscription" on the account details page
	When I click on the "Cancelled" product tab
	Then I should not be able to view the product with the name "DXP Production" on the account details page
	And I should not be able to view the product with the name "Platinum Subscription" on the account details page
	When I click on the "All" product tab
	Then I should be able to view the product with the name "DXP Production" and the following values on the account details page
	| Name                  | DXP Production                                        |
	| Support Life          | ${staticFullStartDate} - ${staticFullOriginalEndDate} |
	| Grace Period End Date | ${staticFullEndDate}                                  |
	| Provisioned           | 1                                                     |
	| Approved Purchased    | 1                                                     |
	| State                 | ACTIVE                                                |
	And I should be able to view the product with the name "DXP Production" under the "Primary" section
	And I should be able to view the product with the name "Platinum Subscription" and the following values on the account details page
	| Name                  | Platinum Subscription                                 |
	| Support Life          | ${staticFullStartDate} - ${staticFullOriginalEndDate} |
	| Grace Period End Date | ${staticFullEndDate}                                  |
	| Provisioned           | 0                                                     |
	| Approved Purchased    | 1                                                     |
	| State                 | ACTIVE                                                |
	And I should be able to view the product with the name "Platinum Subscription" under the "Regular" section
	When I select the following products under the subscriptions tab
	| DXP Production        |
	| Platinum Subscription |
	Then the edit subscriptions button should not be present
	And the subscriptions action dropdown button should not be present
	When I click on the "DXP Production" subscription link
	Then I should be able to view the following subscription values in the subscription details page
	| Name         | DXP Production                                        |
	| State        | ACTIVE                                                |
	| Support Life | ${staticFullStartDate} - ${staticFullOriginalEndDate} |
	| Grace Period | ${staticFullOriginalEndDate} - ${staticFullEndDate}   |
	| Provisioned  | 1                                                     |
	And I should be able to view the term with the start date to end date "${staticFullStartDate} - ${staticFullOriginalEndDate}" and the following values
	| Start - End Date           | ${staticFullStartDate} - ${staticFullOriginalEndDate} |
	| Grace Period               | ${staticFullOriginalEndDate} - ${staticFullEndDate}   |
	| Provisioned                | 1                                                     |
	| Purchased                  | 1                                                     |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Key | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityKey}                     |
	| State                      | ACTIVE                                                |
	And the action dropdown button for the subscription term with the start date to end date "${staticFullStartDate} - ${staticFullOriginalEndDate}" should not be present
	When I go to the account index page
	And I search the accounts page using the keyword "Permis"
	And I click on the account with the name "Permis - ${staticProjectName}" on the provisioning index
	And I click on the "Platinum Subscription" subscription link
	Then I should be able to view the following subscription values in the subscription details page
	| Name         | Platinum Subscription                                 |
	| State        | ACTIVE                                                |
	| Support Life | ${staticFullStartDate} - ${staticFullOriginalEndDate} |
	| Grace Period | ${staticFullOriginalEndDate} - ${staticFullEndDate}   |
	| Provisioned  | 0                                                     |
	And I should be able to view the term with the start date to end date "${staticFullStartDate} - ${staticFullOriginalEndDate}" and the following values
	| Start - End Date           | ${staticFullStartDate} - ${staticFullOriginalEndDate} |
	| Grace Period               | ${staticFullOriginalEndDate} - ${staticFullEndDate}   |
	| Provisioned                | 0                                                     |
	| Purchased                  | 1                                                     |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Key | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityKey}                     |
	| State                      | ACTIVE                                                |
	And the action dropdown button for the subscription term with the start date to end date "${staticFullStartDate} - ${staticFullOriginalEndDate}" should not be present

